Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on practicing MongoDB concepts through basic coding examples. Simple operations such as creating databases, inserting documents, and retrieving data were implemented to understand practical usage. Hands-on exercises were performed to observe how data is stored and managed within collections. This practice helped in connecting theoretical knowledge with real-world implementation.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was improved confidence in performing basic MongoDB operations using code. The practice strengthened understanding of CRUD operations and data handling. It also enhanced the ability to work with collections and documents effectively. Overall, the session contributed to better practical knowledge of MongoDB.
